# `expect(x).to have_event_count(1)` is RSpec's predicate matcher: its
# `method_missing` calls `has_event_count?` on the subject (DEC-090), and
# `--def` said so, but `--refs` and `--dead` counted no such call, so a page
# object's predicate a system spec asserts was `unreferenced`, clear. The
# matcher is a reference to the predicate it calls: confirmed where the
# subject is typed, possible where it is not (`page`), with the present
# tense (`be_exist` → `exists?`) and `be_an_` read as RSpec reads them. A
# matcher RSpec defines (`be_within`) calls no `within?`, and a `have_` call
# outside an example group is no matcher.
